  "conditions": "Each trial repeats an operation on the same prepared pair. One preceding invocation per method is discarded for warm operations. Trial order rotates. Session measures one operator on typed ideals. Prompt measures a named assignment using the prompt evaluator and transcript, excluding terminal I/O. CLI and CLI infix time named and operator assignments through the interactive command loop with input in memory and the terminal panel disabled. It includes routing, multiline detection, evaluation, and transcript updates. First use takes newly declared ideals of the same initialized polynomials without a warm-up per ideal. Declare and first use includes construction of the input ideals from those polynomials. First declaration on fresh polynomials excludes creation of the separate rings and polynomial values, and includes their very first ideal construction. Script with declarations evaluates named functions and binds I, J as needed and answer through the shared script evaluator, submitted once per iteration. Direct named assignments use the same public functions and workspace dictionary in Python. The Atlas loop runs the same statements inside a single script for-loop over a prepared tuple, after one untimed iteration. Record measures first export of a complete record from an already computed result. Native wire includes sparse input decoding and JSON output. Prepared native measures C++ arithmetic on parsed inputs and the completed result stays in memory. Singular measures an assignment on initialized ideals in its interpreter, with one thread. Timings exclude top-level program startup, input declarations, and agreement checks. Each trial checks mutual containment in Singular. Ordinary power returns a reduced basis in Atlas, so Singular uses std(I^2) with option(redSB).",
